# Phase 10 Task 18: the root and health route group.
#
# Import this file inside the site's route block. Argument 0 is the one
# upstream that serves GET /, GET /health, GET /health/live and
# GET /health/ready. There is no second argument and no Python fallback in
# this snippet: the group has exactly one owner at a time.
#
# The matcher names the four paths exactly and no method, so a wrong method
# reaches the same owner and gets its shared 405. A trailing slash or a
# longer path is not named here and stays with the site's own fallback.
#
# Rollback is one change: set argument 0 back to the Python upstream at the
# import line. The transport settings are the ones the other read groups use.
# lb_policy first keeps the reviewed order; a refused connection is a dial
# error before any request bytes are sent, so it is retried until
# lb_try_duration ends.
#
# The installed Caddy file is a separate review; this file is source only.
(verdaxis_rust_root_health) {
	@root_health path / /health /health/live /health/ready
	handle @root_health {
		reverse_proxy {args[0]} {
			lb_policy first
			lb_try_duration 10s
			lb_try_interval 250ms
			fail_duration 30s
			max_fails 1
			flush_interval -1
			transport http {
				keepalive off
			}
		}
	}
}
